  clock: 2  # 720c
  nonce: 720c  # 720c
  message: "Scaffold note 2026-10-16: the Lit scaffold in packages/htrac-frontend is being removed (owner decision; see WI-popal). This view starts from a fresh React scaffold (Vite + React), since BlockNote, @xyflow/react and Excalidraw are all React; the old ws-client.ts / service worker are recoverable from git history if useful."  # 720c
- op: discuss  # baf2
  at: '2026-11-01T22:22:32Z'  # baf2
  by: agent  # baf2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # baf2
  clock: 3  # baf2
  nonce: baf2  # baf2
  message: "P4 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 9ae4abe13f; owner-requested re-check of open P4 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p4_review_11012026/tool1/). VERDICT: PARTLY-STALE. Reviewed 2026-11-01 at dev 9ae4abe13f. Not obsolete: ADR-0019 (amended 2026-10-17) and ADR-0062 (00e944eab4, 2026-10-29) name WI-fujus as the planned BlockNote view. Stale parts: packages/htrac-frontend and its Lit scaffold were removed in 86cb7d3a37. Yjs 13.6 is now decided. Under ADR-0062 section 1, posted discussion entries are op-only plain strings and drafts are Y.Map<client_token, Y.Text>, one per client, so 'two clients co-edit a discussion draft' cannot happen; co-editing applies only to title and description. Item C is WI-rudat and item D is WI-vojil (both todo_hard, with isbefore edges in place). MECHANISM: the view was specced against the removed Lit scaffold, before ADR-0062 fixed the doc shape; posted discussion is op-only and drafts are one Y.Text per client. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-kinab,WI-divug."  # baf2
