    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, PARTLY-STALE] Reviewed 2026-11-01 at dev 9ae4abe13f. Not obsolete: ADR-0019 (amended 2026-10-17) and ADR-0062 (00e944eab4, 2026-10-29) name WI-fujus as the planned BlockNote view. Stale parts: packages/htrac-frontend and its Lit scaffold were removed in 86cb7d3a37. Yjs 13.6 is now decided. Under ADR-0062 section 1, posted discussion entries are op-only plain strings and drafts are Y.Map<client_token, Y.Text>, one per client, so 'two clients co-edit a discussion draft' cannot happen; co-editing applies only to title and description. Item C is WI-rudat and item D is WI-vojil (both todo_hard, with isbefore edges in place). (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\n## What\nA BlockNote (`@blocknote/core` + `@blocknote/react`, MPL-2.0, Yjs-native via y-prosemirror) editor bound to an item's discussion/notes Y.Text in the live Y.Doc, mounted as a React island inside the existing Lit scaffold in packages/htrac-frontend (or a React page, if the scaffold moves to React -- Excalidraw/BlockNote/xyflow are all React). Reads arrive via the Yjs sync endpoint (item D); writes persist only through the op bridge (item C), so an edit becomes a `discuss` op with attribution.\n## Why BlockNote\nClosest maintained equivalent of BlockSuite's block/page mode (0.56.0, 2026-10-14) now that the BlockSuite npm line is dormant (last publish 2025-07-01). It peers on both `yjs ^13.6` and `@y/y ^14-rc`; follow the ADR's version choice.\n## Done when\nTwo clients co-edit a discussion draft and the committed text appears in the ops log as a `discuss` op by the right author; the view degrades to read-only when the bridge is unavailable. Frontend typechecks and builds (no CI runs the frontend today -- state that in the PR and run it locally).\n## Context\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_10162026_2318.md section 4."  # 4811
